1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,710
Léa: Hello everyone!

2
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:03,560
Welcome to The Cozy French,

3
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:05,200
your little get-together

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,780
to learn French

5
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:08,930
through natural

6
00:00:08,930 --> 00:00:10,040
and warm conversations.

7
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:11,830
I'm Léa, and I'm very happy

8
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:13,740
to be with you again today.

9
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:15,080
Mathieu: And I'm Mathieu!

10
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:16,330
Hello, dear friends!

11
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:18,140
Whether you're at home,

12
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:19,040
on public transport

13
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:21,240
or making your coffee,

14
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:23,200
get comfortable.

15
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,900
We're delighted to spend this time with you.

16
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:27,970
Léa: Mathieu, I have a question for you.

17
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:29,400
Do you consider yourself

18
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,330
a disciplined person?

19
00:00:31,380 --> 00:00:34,080
Mathieu: Hmm... It depends on the day.

20
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:37,240
On Mondays, I'm usually very disciplined.

21
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,580
On Fridays, it's another story.

22
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:41,130
Léa: Really? Why?

23
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:42,440
Mathieu: Because on Mondays,

24
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:44,480
I'm full of good intentions.

25
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:47,340
I want to work efficiently, exercise,

26
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:50,380
read more and take care of myself.

27
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:52,200
But after a few days,

28
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,200
my enthusiasm starts to fade.

29
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:56,900
Léa: I think a lot of people

30
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:58,540
know this situation.

31
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:00,430
You make a nice plan,

32
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:02,280
then you struggle to stick to it.

33
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:03,980
Mathieu: Exactly.

34
00:01:04,030 --> 00:01:06,060
And sometimes, my brain comes up with

35
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:08,680
such convincing excuses

36
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:10,880
that I end up believing it's right.

37
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,240
Léa: Give me an example.

38
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:13,810
Mathieu: For two weeks now,

39
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:15,440
I've had to tidy the papers

40
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,380
piling up on my desk.

41
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:20,600
Every evening, I tell myself I'll deal with it.

42
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:22,680
But as soon as I get home,

43
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:24,110
a little voice tells me:

44
00:01:24,110 --> 00:01:26,540
"You've worked all day.

45
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:27,580
Do it tomorrow."

46
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:29,080
Léa: And tomorrow comes...

47
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:31,100
Mathieu: And that little voice comes back

48
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,080
with a new argument!

49
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:34,830
It's very creative, you know.

50
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:38,080
Léa: That's a great introduction to our topic.

51
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:40,110
Today, we're going to talk

52
00:01:40,110 --> 00:01:41,640
about mental discipline

53
00:01:41,640 --> 00:01:43,940
and how we can learn

54
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:45,780
to better manage our habits,

55
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:48,000
our attention and our decisions.

56
00:01:48,050 --> 00:01:49,540
Mathieu: But careful, dear friends,

57
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:50,840
we're not going to tell you

58
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,440
to work non-stop

59
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,240
or to become machines!

60
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:55,450
Léa: Absolutely not.

61
00:01:55,500 --> 00:01:58,540
Being disciplined doesn't mean punishing yourself.

62
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:00,590
It means learning instead

63
00:02:00,590 --> 00:02:02,670
to do what matters to us,

64
00:02:02,670 --> 00:02:04,740
even when our mood changes.

65
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:06,780
Mathieu: And also learning to recognise

66
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:09,340
when we really need rest.

67
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:10,550
Léa: Exactly.

68
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:12,640
As always, we'll discover

69
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,940
useful French expressions

70
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:17,440
and share a few everyday stories.

71
00:02:17,490 --> 00:02:18,460
Mathieu: Before we start,

72
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:20,240
tell us in the comments:

73
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,340
what's one thing

74
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:23,640
you often put off until tomorrow?

75
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:25,640
A short sentence in French is enough.

76
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:27,900
Léa: And if you enjoy learning with us,

77
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:30,540
remember to subscribe to The Cozy French.

78
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:32,090
Now, let's begin!

79
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,400
Mathieu: So, Léa,

80
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,770
why does our mind prefer

81
00:02:35,770 --> 00:02:37,840
to often do something else

82
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,590
than what we had planned?

83
00:02:39,640 --> 00:02:41,470
Léa: Because some activities

84
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:43,700
give us instant pleasure,

85
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:45,950
while others require effort

86
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:48,140
before they give us a result.

87
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:49,530
Mathieu: Like watching a video

88
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:51,490
instead of tidying my papers?

89
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:52,590
Léa: Exactly.

90
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:55,840
Watching a video is easy and pleasant.

91
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:58,780
Tidying your papers means starting a task

92
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,340
you probably find boring.

93
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:02,390
Mathieu: That's true.

94
00:03:02,440 --> 00:03:05,740
And my excuses always seem reasonable.

95
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:07,940
I tell myself I'm tired,

96
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,440
that it's not urgent

97
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:12,500
or that I'll be more efficient at the weekend.

98
00:03:12,550 --> 00:03:14,740
Léa: Sometimes, those reasons are valid.

99
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:17,270
But sometimes, they simply serve

100
00:03:17,270 --> 00:03:19,640
to avoid an unpleasant activity.

101
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,380
Mathieu: So I need to learn

102
00:03:21,380 --> 00:03:23,280
to recognise the difference

103
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:26,140
between a real need for rest

104
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:29,040
and a simple urge to put the task off.

105
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,290
Léa: Exactly.

106
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:32,940
And you can start by asking yourself:

107
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:35,530
"Has something important changed

108
00:03:35,530 --> 00:03:37,790
since I made this decision?"

109
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:39,940
Mathieu: For example, if I'm sick,

110
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:42,000
I can change my plan.

111
00:03:42,050 --> 00:03:43,910
But if I just feel like

112
00:03:43,910 --> 00:03:45,940
watching another video,

113
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:48,640
maybe I can keep my commitment.

114
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:49,590
Léa: Absolutely.

115
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:52,930
It doesn't mean ignoring what you feel,

116
00:03:52,930 --> 00:03:55,440
but choosing your reaction more consciously.

117
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:58,370
Mathieu: You know, I sometimes spend twenty minutes

118
00:03:58,370 --> 00:04:01,140
wondering whether to start a task

119
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:03,240
that would only take ten minutes.

120
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,490
Léa: Oh yes! That's quite ironic.

121
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:07,720
You spend more energy

122
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:10,200
avoiding the work than doing it.

123
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,090
Mathieu: Exactly. And then,

124
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:15,340
I feel guilty for not having started.

125
00:04:15,340 --> 00:04:17,670
Léa: So maybe you should make

126
00:04:17,670 --> 00:04:19,640
the start much simpler.

127
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:20,590
Mathieu: How?

128
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:21,650
Léa: Instead of saying

129
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:23,970
"I'm going to tidy my whole desk",

130
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:25,450
simply decide:

131
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:26,940
"I'll sort the papers

132
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:29,290
for ten minutes after my coffee."

133
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:30,990
Mathieu: Only ten minutes?

134
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:34,290
Léa: Yes. And if you want to keep going, you can.

135
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:37,960
But your initial goal stays ten minutes.

136
00:04:38,010 --> 00:04:40,590
Mathieu: That's much less daunting.

137
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:44,840
When I think of tidying everything, I feel swamped.

138
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:48,340
But ten minutes seems doable.

139
00:04:48,340 --> 00:04:51,310
Léa: That's it. Often, the hard part is

140
00:04:51,310 --> 00:04:53,240
in the first few minutes.

141
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:55,380
Once we've started,

142
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,740
the task can become easier.

143
00:04:57,740 --> 00:05:00,240
Mathieu: I've noticed that with walks.

144
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:02,370
Sometimes, I stay on my sofa

145
00:05:02,370 --> 00:05:03,920
for twenty minutes

146
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:06,440
telling myself I should go out.

147
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:07,700
Léa: And in the end?

148
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:09,400
Mathieu: When I put my shoes on

149
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,140
and step out the door,

150
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:13,440
I'm happy to be outside.

151
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:15,730
Léa: So the first obstacle was

152
00:05:15,730 --> 00:05:17,740
simply getting started.

153
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:19,290
Mathieu: Exactly.

154
00:05:19,340 --> 00:05:22,680
My brain had turned a little walk

155
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:25,040
into a very complicated mission.

156
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:27,880
Léa: And that brings us to an interesting word:

157
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,840
"resistance".

158
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,060
In this context,

159
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:34,120
it's that inner feeling that pushes us

160
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:37,200
to avoid something that takes effort.

161
00:05:37,250 --> 00:05:40,840
Mathieu: For example: "I feel a lot of resistance

162
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:43,840
when I have to start a difficult project."

163
00:05:43,840 --> 00:05:44,590
Léa: Very good.

164
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:47,040
But feeling that resistance

165
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,820
doesn't automatically mean

166
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:50,640
we have to give up.

167
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:53,940
Mathieu: We can admit a task is unpleasant

168
00:05:53,940 --> 00:05:57,840
and still decide to start gently.

169
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:59,190
Léa: Exactly.

170
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,040
And sometimes, the desire comes

171
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:03,700
after the first few minutes of action.

172
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:04,620
Mathieu: That reassures me,

173
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:07,350
because I often wait to feel motivated

174
00:06:07,350 --> 00:06:09,640
before doing anything at all.

175
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:11,380
Léa: Yet motivation

176
00:06:11,380 --> 00:06:13,440
isn't always there.

177
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:15,650
If we rely only on it,

178
00:06:15,650 --> 00:06:16,880
it becomes hard

179
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:19,540
to build regular habits.

180
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:23,180
Mathieu: True. When I start a new project,

181
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:26,140
the first days are always exciting.

182
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:29,700
Then the activity becomes more ordinary.

183
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:32,620
Léa: And it's precisely on those ordinary days

184
00:06:32,620 --> 00:06:35,140
that consistency becomes important.

185
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:37,130
Mathieu: You know, when I was a student,

186
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:39,640
I tried to learn the guitar.

187
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,340
At first, I was so enthusiastic

188
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:44,640
that I practised every evening.

189
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:45,120
Léa: Really?

190
00:06:45,170 --> 00:06:47,790
I didn't know you played the guitar.

191
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,680
Mathieu: I wouldn't exactly say

192
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:51,540
that I play the guitar.

193
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:55,170
Let's say I developed a complicated relationship

194
00:06:55,170 --> 00:06:56,910
with three chords.

195
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:58,050
Léa: Mathieu!

196
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,590
Mathieu: It's true!

197
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:01,640
After a few weeks,

198
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,140
I realised

199
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:05,460
I had to repeat the same movements

200
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:07,140
over and over again.

201
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:09,030
It was much less fun

202
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:10,840
than I had imagined.

203
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:13,550
Léa: You mostly loved the idea of being able to play,

204
00:07:13,550 --> 00:07:15,620
but not necessarily all the steps

205
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,640
to learn.

206
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:17,850
Mathieu: Exactly.

207
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:21,140
I could already see myself playing lovely songs,

208
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,780
but I hadn't pictured the evenings

209
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:26,200
practising the same chords.

210
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:27,080
Léa: And yet,

211
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:30,140
those repetitions are part of the process.

212
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:33,340
Mathieu: Yes. I think I needed to accept

213
00:07:33,340 --> 00:07:35,970
that a project can't be exciting

214
00:07:35,970 --> 00:07:37,140
every single moment.

215
00:07:37,140 --> 00:07:39,140
Léa: That's a lovely thought.

216
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:41,170
Discipline sometimes helps us

217
00:07:41,170 --> 00:07:44,140
keep going once the novelty has gone.

218
00:07:44,140 --> 00:07:45,740
Mathieu: And it also works

219
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:47,840
for learning French.

220
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:49,760
At first, you're happy

221
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:52,200
to discover new words.

222
00:07:52,250 --> 00:07:53,900
But after a few months,

223
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,640
progress sometimes seems slower.

224
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:57,590
Léa: Exactly.

225
00:07:57,640 --> 00:08:00,640
You have to listen to some conversations again,

226
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:02,240
review expressions

227
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:04,640
and accept making mistakes.

228
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:06,240
Mathieu: And that's exactly where

229
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:09,640
a regular habit becomes precious.

230
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:12,640
Léa: Yes. Not necessarily two hours every day.

231
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:15,640
Fifteen or twenty minutes can already help

232
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:18,200
if that fits our life.

233
00:08:18,250 --> 00:08:20,890
Mathieu: You know, for a long time I thought

234
00:08:20,890 --> 00:08:23,140
discipline meant

235
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:25,140
doing big things.

236
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,940
Léa: Whereas it's often about

237
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:29,140
keeping small commitments.

238
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:30,000
Mathieu: The promises

239
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,140
we make to ourselves?

240
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:36,140
Léa: Exactly. When you decide to read five pages,

241
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,140
and then you do it,

242
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:39,750
you gradually build trust

243
00:08:39,750 --> 00:08:42,140
in your own decisions.

244
00:08:42,140 --> 00:08:43,900
Mathieu: And if I always promise

245
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:47,200
to do something without ever doing it,

246
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:49,140
that trust can shrink.

247
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:51,510
Léa: Yes. That's why it's better to choose

248
00:08:51,510 --> 00:08:53,140
realistic commitments

249
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:56,140
rather than make impossible plans.

250
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,850
Mathieu: So, instead of saying

251
00:08:57,900 --> 00:09:01,090
"I'll read thirty pages every evening",

252
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:04,140
I can start with five pages.

253
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:08,140
Léa: Absolutely. Some evenings, you'll read more.

254
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:12,140
Other evenings, five pages will be enough.

255
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:15,200
Mathieu: But what if I miss a day?

256
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:17,140
Léa: You can simply start again.

257
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,230
A missed day

258
00:09:18,230 --> 00:09:20,140
doesn't destroy all your progress.

259
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:21,900
Mathieu: Ah, that's something

260
00:09:21,900 --> 00:09:24,140
I find hard to accept.

261
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:26,140
When I miss a day,

262
00:09:26,140 --> 00:09:27,740
I sometimes feel

263
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:30,140
that my whole plan is completely ruined.

264
00:09:30,140 --> 00:09:33,140
Léa: That's a very rigid way of thinking.

265
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:34,740
We tend to believe

266
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,140
that everything must be perfect,

267
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:38,660
while a habit can stay

268
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:41,200
useful even with a few interruptions.

269
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:42,730
Mathieu: So I don't need

270
00:09:42,730 --> 00:09:45,090
to start all over again.

271
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:48,140
Léa: Exactly. And there's another way

272
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:50,140
to make our good habits easier:

273
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:53,140
organising our environment.

274
00:09:53,140 --> 00:09:55,090
Mathieu: Our environment?

275
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:57,090
You mean my flat?

276
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:57,570
Léa: Yes.

277
00:09:57,570 --> 00:09:59,140
The objects around us

278
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,140
can influence our behaviour.

279
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:05,140
For example, if your phone is right in front of you

280
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:06,140
while you're reading,

281
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:08,170
you're likely to get distracted.

282
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:09,120
Mathieu: That's true.

283
00:10:09,170 --> 00:10:10,800
Sometimes I pick it up

284
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:13,140
without even realising.

285
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:15,450
Léa: Then you can just leave it

286
00:10:15,450 --> 00:10:18,140
in another room while you read.

287
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:19,740
Mathieu: So I don't need

288
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:21,140
to spend fifteen minutes

289
00:10:21,140 --> 00:10:23,140
resisting temptation.

290
00:10:23,140 --> 00:10:26,140
I can reduce the distraction.

291
00:10:26,140 --> 00:10:29,140
Léa: Exactly. It's much simpler

292
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:32,140
than relying only on your willpower.

293
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:34,140
Mathieu: I like that idea.

294
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:35,730
It reminds me of something

295
00:10:35,730 --> 00:10:37,200
I tried recently.

296
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:40,780
I wanted to read more, so I started

297
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:44,140
leaving my book near my sofa.

298
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:46,090
Léa: And does it work?

299
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:47,740
Mathieu: Yes! Before,

300
00:10:47,740 --> 00:10:51,140
my book was put away on a bookshelf.

301
00:10:51,140 --> 00:10:54,140
Now, it's always within reach,

302
00:10:54,140 --> 00:10:56,140
and I pick it up much more often.

303
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:57,090
Léa: There you go.

304
00:10:57,140 --> 00:11:00,140
A small change in our environment

305
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:03,200
can sometimes make a real difference.

306
00:11:03,250 --> 00:11:04,740
Mathieu: We can also get

307
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:07,140
our sports shoes ready the night before

308
00:11:07,140 --> 00:11:11,140
or keep our work papers well organised.

309
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:15,140
Léa: Exactly. And if you want to practise French,

310
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:16,940
you can prepare a list

311
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:20,140
of podcasts or conversations to listen to.

312
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:22,090
Mathieu: Like The Cozy French!

313
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,090
Léa: Of course!

314
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:25,280
Mathieu: You know, that changes the way

315
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:27,140
I see discipline.

316
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:28,900
Instead of asking myself

317
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:32,200
how to become mentally stronger,

318
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:33,740
I can also look for ways

319
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:37,140
to make good decisions easier.

320
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:40,340
Léa: That's it. Discipline isn't always

321
00:11:40,340 --> 00:11:42,140
a fight against yourself.

322
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:43,900
Mathieu: But there's something else

323
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:46,140
I'd like to understand.

324
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:49,140
How do you know when to keep going

325
00:11:49,140 --> 00:11:51,090
and when to stop?

326
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:53,140
Léa: That's an essential question.

327
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:55,140
Because being disciplined

328
00:11:55,140 --> 00:11:58,200
doesn't mean working until exhaustion.

329
00:11:58,250 --> 00:12:00,500
Mathieu: Yet some people think

330
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:03,140
you should always push yourself harder.

331
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:04,740
Léa: But imagine you've been working

332
00:12:04,740 --> 00:12:06,140
for several hours.

333
00:12:06,140 --> 00:12:08,420
You're tired, you're making mistakes

334
00:12:08,420 --> 00:12:11,140
and you can no longer concentrate.

335
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,180
Mathieu: In that case,

336
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:16,140
carrying on isn't necessarily very efficient.

337
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:17,090
Léa: Exactly.

338
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:20,140
Sometimes, the most responsible decision

339
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:22,140
is to take a break

340
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:24,200
or to end your day.

341
00:12:24,250 --> 00:12:25,960
Mathieu: That reminds me of an evening

342
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:29,140
when I was working on a presentation.

343
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:31,240
I was so tired

344
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:33,620
that I kept rereading the same sentence

345
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:36,140
without managing to understand it.

346
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:38,090
Léa: And what did you do?

347
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:41,140
Mathieu: In the end, I decided to go to sleep.

348
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:42,760
The next morning,

349
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:45,720
I finished in twenty minutes a part

350
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,140
that had seemed impossible the night before.

351
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:48,680
Léa: There you go.

352
00:12:48,730 --> 00:12:51,340
Your problem wasn't necessarily

353
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:53,200
a lack of discipline.

354
00:12:53,250 --> 00:12:56,140
You simply needed rest.

355
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:59,430
Mathieu: So you have to tell the normal discomfort

356
00:12:59,430 --> 00:13:03,140
of a hard task apart from real tiredness.

357
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:06,340
Léa: Exactly. It's not always easy,

358
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:08,340
but we can learn

359
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:11,140
to observe our state and our needs.

360
00:13:11,140 --> 00:13:13,700
Mathieu: You know, I really like this idea

361
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:17,200
of a firm but kind discipline.

362
00:13:17,250 --> 00:13:17,640
Léa: Yes.

363
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:21,800
"Kind" means acting with gentleness,

364
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,140
understanding and respect.

365
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:26,310
And it can also apply to the way

366
00:13:26,310 --> 00:13:28,140
we talk to ourselves inside.

367
00:13:28,140 --> 00:13:31,140
Mathieu: For example, instead of saying

368
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:34,140
"I'm incapable of keeping my commitments",

369
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:35,260
I could say

370
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:37,580
"I didn't manage today.

371
00:13:37,580 --> 00:13:40,210
What can I improve?"

372
00:13:40,260 --> 00:13:41,350
Léa: Exactly.

373
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:44,430
The second sentence looks for a solution

374
00:13:44,430 --> 00:13:48,140
rather than creating more guilt.

375
00:13:48,140 --> 00:13:50,080
Mathieu: And it makes me much more eager

376
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,140
to start again.

377
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:53,090
Léa: That's important.

378
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:56,140
We can acknowledge our responsibilities

379
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:59,140
without always being harsh on ourselves.

380
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,990
Mathieu: You know, that makes me think

381
00:14:00,990 --> 00:14:04,200
of another difficulty: losing your rhythm.

382
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:04,880
Léa: Oh yes.

383
00:14:04,930 --> 00:14:07,610
When you've kept a good habit

384
00:14:07,610 --> 00:14:10,140
for several weeks,

385
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:13,140
and then something interrupts your routine.

386
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:15,410
Mathieu: Exactly. Last year,

387
00:14:15,410 --> 00:14:18,140
I used to walk regularly after dinner.

388
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:20,760
Then I had a very busy week

389
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:23,140
and I stopped completely.

390
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:25,090
Léa: And how did you get back into it?

391
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:27,980
Mathieu: For several days, I told myself:

392
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:30,140
"I'll start again on Monday."

393
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:31,490
But Monday would come,

394
00:14:31,490 --> 00:14:35,140
and I always found a new excuse.

395
00:14:35,140 --> 00:14:37,090
Léa: Why wait for Monday?

396
00:14:37,140 --> 00:14:38,060
Mathieu: That's exactly

397
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:40,140
what I finally asked myself!

398
00:14:40,140 --> 00:14:43,190
One Thursday, I just put my shoes on

399
00:14:43,190 --> 00:14:46,140
and went out for a twenty-minute walk.

400
00:14:46,140 --> 00:14:47,720
Léa: And that little walk helped you

401
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,090
get your habit back.

402
00:14:49,140 --> 00:14:52,090
Mathieu: Yes. Nothing spectacular.

403
00:14:52,140 --> 00:14:55,140
No new plan, no big decision.

404
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:57,200
I simply started again.

405
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:58,690
Léa: That's a lovely lesson.

406
00:14:58,740 --> 00:15:00,010
We don't need

407
00:15:00,010 --> 00:15:02,140
to wait for a special occasion

408
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:04,140
to get back to something important.

409
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:06,120
Mathieu: In French, we can say

410
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:09,140
"reprendre là où on s'était arrêté".

411
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:10,090
Léa: Exactly.

412
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:13,680
This expression means restarting an activity

413
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:15,140
after a break,

414
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:18,200
without necessarily starting from scratch.

415
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:19,050
Mathieu: For example:

416
00:15:19,050 --> 00:15:21,340
"I stopped studying French

417
00:15:21,340 --> 00:15:23,120
for a few weeks,

418
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:24,630
but now, I'm going to

419
00:15:24,630 --> 00:15:27,140
pick up where I left off."

420
00:15:27,140 --> 00:15:28,970
Léa: And that's especially important

421
00:15:28,970 --> 00:15:30,140
for our listeners.

422
00:15:30,140 --> 00:15:32,130
Maybe some of you

423
00:15:32,130 --> 00:15:34,140
have paused your learning

424
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:35,370
because of work

425
00:15:35,370 --> 00:15:38,140
or family responsibilities.

426
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:40,590
Mathieu: But you can come back calmly,

427
00:15:40,590 --> 00:15:41,770
without blaming yourself

428
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:44,200
for all the time spent not practising.

429
00:15:44,250 --> 00:15:47,180
Léa: Yes. You can review some things,

430
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:48,780
find your rhythm again

431
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:51,140
and keep going step by step.

432
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:52,400
Mathieu: You know, I think

433
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:54,830
true discipline also shows

434
00:15:54,830 --> 00:15:58,140
in the moments when nobody's watching.

435
00:15:58,140 --> 00:15:59,090
Léa: What do you mean?

436
00:15:59,140 --> 00:16:01,980
Mathieu: If I decide to study ten minutes tonight,

437
00:16:01,980 --> 00:16:05,140
nobody will necessarily know if I did it.

438
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:08,200
Léa: True. But you will know.

439
00:16:08,250 --> 00:16:09,030
Mathieu: Exactly.

440
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:11,860
And when I keep that little promise,

441
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:14,380
I feel like I'm becoming someone

442
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:16,140
I can count on.

443
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:18,140
Léa: I really like that idea.

444
00:16:18,140 --> 00:16:20,120
Discipline isn't only about

445
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:22,140
reaching visible goals.

446
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:23,410
It also helps us

447
00:16:23,410 --> 00:16:25,790
build a more reliable relationship

448
00:16:25,790 --> 00:16:27,140
with ourselves.

449
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:29,710
Mathieu: And that builds up gradually,

450
00:16:29,710 --> 00:16:32,200
with small repeated actions.

451
00:16:32,250 --> 00:16:34,980
Léa: Exactly. But we also have to accept

452
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:38,140
that our habits change with our life.

453
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:40,040
Mathieu: Because some people

454
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:43,140
prefer studying in the morning, others at night.

455
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:46,140
Léa: Yes. Some have a lot of free time,

456
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:48,350
others have to juggle work,

457
00:16:48,350 --> 00:16:50,140
studies or children.

458
00:16:50,140 --> 00:16:53,520
Mathieu: So there's no single perfect routine

459
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:55,200
for everyone.

460
00:16:55,250 --> 00:16:58,020
Léa: Absolutely. The best plan is the one

461
00:16:58,020 --> 00:16:59,780
that fits our needs

462
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:01,550
and that we can adapt

463
00:17:01,550 --> 00:17:04,140
when our circumstances change.

464
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:04,950
Mathieu: You know, Léa,

465
00:17:04,950 --> 00:17:08,140
I think I finally understand something.

466
00:17:08,140 --> 00:17:09,270
Being disciplined

467
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:11,780
doesn't mean never wanting

468
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:13,140
to procrastinate.

469
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:15,290
Léa: No. It means learning

470
00:17:15,290 --> 00:17:17,290
to recognise your habits

471
00:17:17,290 --> 00:17:20,200
and to make more conscious choices.

472
00:17:20,250 --> 00:17:23,770
Mathieu: And sometimes, choosing to start gently.

473
00:17:23,770 --> 00:17:27,060
Sometimes, choosing to rest. And sometimes,

474
00:17:27,060 --> 00:17:30,140
simply starting again after a break.

475
00:17:30,140 --> 00:17:32,140
Léa: Exactly.

476
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:34,200
Now, I suggest we review

477
00:17:34,200 --> 00:17:37,140
a few important French expressions.

478
00:17:37,140 --> 00:17:38,350
Mathieu: Great idea!

479
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:41,200
Let's start with "remettre au lendemain".

480
00:17:41,250 --> 00:17:42,870
Léa: "Remettre au lendemain"

481
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:46,200
means putting a task off until later.

482
00:17:46,250 --> 00:17:47,060
For example:

483
00:17:47,060 --> 00:17:49,140
"I always put off tidying

484
00:17:49,140 --> 00:17:51,140
my desk until tomorrow."

485
00:17:51,140 --> 00:17:55,090
Mathieu: Second expression: "se trouver des excuses".

486
00:17:55,140 --> 00:17:57,030
Léa: It means looking for reasons

487
00:17:57,030 --> 00:17:59,140
to avoid doing something.

488
00:17:59,140 --> 00:18:00,130
For example:

489
00:18:00,130 --> 00:18:02,830
"Every time I have to exercise,

490
00:18:02,830 --> 00:18:06,140
I find an excuse to stay at home."

491
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:08,200
Mathieu: Third expression: "s'y mettre".

492
00:18:08,250 --> 00:18:12,200
Léa: "S'y mettre" means starting an activity.

493
00:18:12,250 --> 00:18:12,980
For example:

494
00:18:12,980 --> 00:18:14,180
"I've wanted to learn the piano

495
00:18:14,180 --> 00:18:16,140
for a long time.

496
00:18:16,140 --> 00:18:19,140
I really should get down to it."

497
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:22,090
Mathieu: Fourth expression: "tenir ses engagements".

498
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:25,080
Léa: It means doing what you promised

499
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,090
or decided.

500
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:27,160
For example:

501
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:30,430
"I try to choose realistic goals

502
00:18:30,430 --> 00:18:33,140
to better keep my commitments."

503
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:35,090
Mathieu: Fifth expression: "perdre le rythme".

504
00:18:35,140 --> 00:18:37,210
Léa: It means no longer managing

505
00:18:37,210 --> 00:18:40,200
to keep a habit up regularly.

506
00:18:40,250 --> 00:18:41,130
For example:

507
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:43,980
"After the holidays, I lost the rhythm

508
00:18:43,980 --> 00:18:46,140
of my French sessions."

509
00:18:46,140 --> 00:18:48,750
Mathieu: And our last expression:

510
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:52,090
"reprendre là où on s'était arrêté".

511
00:18:52,140 --> 00:18:56,090
Léa: It means starting again after a break.

512
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:57,180
For example:

513
00:18:57,180 --> 00:18:59,450
"After a hard week,

514
00:18:59,450 --> 00:19:03,210
I picked my project up where I'd left off."

515
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:05,730
Mathieu: That's six very useful expressions.

516
00:19:05,730 --> 00:19:08,850
And now, how about we look at how

517
00:19:08,850 --> 00:19:12,140
to make some sentences sound more natural?

518
00:19:12,140 --> 00:19:13,090
Léa: Great idea.

519
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:17,090
Let's start with: "I'll do that later."

520
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:18,020
Mathieu: You can say:

521
00:19:18,070 --> 00:19:21,160
"I'll deal with it tonight." Or:

522
00:19:21,210 --> 00:19:22,850
"I'll take ten minutes

523
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:25,090
to sort that out after lunch."

524
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:27,670
Léa: These sentences are more precise

525
00:19:27,670 --> 00:19:31,200
and give the task a concrete time.

526
00:19:31,250 --> 00:19:32,490
Mathieu: Second sentence:

527
00:19:32,540 --> 00:19:35,090
"I don't feel like doing it."

528
00:19:35,140 --> 00:19:36,130
Léa: You can say:

529
00:19:36,180 --> 00:19:39,390
"I'm struggling to get started today." Or:

530
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:41,290
"I'm not very motivated,

531
00:19:41,290 --> 00:19:44,090
but I'll start gently."

532
00:19:44,140 --> 00:19:48,090
Mathieu: Third sentence: "I'm not disciplined."

533
00:19:48,140 --> 00:19:49,100
Léa: You can say:

534
00:19:49,150 --> 00:19:50,530
"I still struggle

535
00:19:50,530 --> 00:19:53,340
to keep a regular routine." Or:

536
00:19:53,380 --> 00:19:55,060
"I'm trying to develop

537
00:19:55,060 --> 00:19:57,200
better habits."

538
00:19:57,250 --> 00:20:01,090
Mathieu: Fourth sentence: "I failed again."

539
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:01,930
Léa: You can say:

540
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:03,050
"I didn't manage

541
00:20:03,050 --> 00:20:05,430
to stick to my plan this week,

542
00:20:05,430 --> 00:20:07,090
but I can start again."

543
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:09,140
Mathieu: Or: "I've lost my rhythm,

544
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:13,090
but I'll gradually get back into it."

545
00:20:13,140 --> 00:20:14,960
Léa: And our last sentence:

546
00:20:15,010 --> 00:20:18,090
"I need to be stricter with myself."

547
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:19,080
Mathieu: You can say:

548
00:20:19,130 --> 00:20:22,640
"I need to be more honest with myself,

549
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:25,210
without judging myself too harshly."

550
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:27,090
Léa: Exactly.

551
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,430
We can recognise our difficulties

552
00:20:29,430 --> 00:20:31,140
without getting even more discouraged.

553
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:34,140
Mathieu: You know, Léa, after this conversation,

554
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:36,750
I think I've finally found a solution

555
00:20:36,750 --> 00:20:38,140
for my papers.

556
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:41,090
Léa: Oh really? Back to your famous desk!

557
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:43,530
Mathieu: Yes. Tonight, after dinner,

558
00:20:43,530 --> 00:20:47,140
I'll sort my papers for ten minutes.

559
00:20:47,140 --> 00:20:51,200
Léa: That's a precise and realistic commitment.

560
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,120
Mathieu: And if I haven't finished,

561
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:56,140
I can carry on another day.

562
00:20:56,140 --> 00:20:57,160
Léa: Exactly.

563
00:20:57,210 --> 00:20:59,930
No need to turn this tidy-up

564
00:20:59,930 --> 00:21:02,140
into an extraordinary mission.

565
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:04,230
Mathieu: I'll even get a little box ready

566
00:21:04,230 --> 00:21:06,140
to organise the papers.

567
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:07,350
Léa: Great idea.

568
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:10,140
You're making the task easier to start.

569
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:14,140
Mathieu: See, I'm becoming a disciplined person!

570
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:15,480
Léa: Easy, Mathieu.

571
00:21:15,480 --> 00:21:16,600
Let's wait and see

572
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:19,200
if the papers really get tidied!

573
00:21:19,250 --> 00:21:21,140
Mathieu: You don't trust me?

574
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:22,550
Léa: Let's say I prefer

575
00:21:22,550 --> 00:21:25,140
actions to big promises!

576
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:28,140
Mathieu: Fair enough. And you, dear friends,

577
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:29,400
what small action

578
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:31,140
could you take today

579
00:21:31,140 --> 00:21:34,090
to move towards an important goal?

580
00:21:34,140 --> 00:21:37,140
Léa: Maybe listen to a few minutes of French,

581
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:40,730
tidy a small space, read a few pages

582
00:21:40,730 --> 00:21:42,650
or get back to an activity

583
00:21:42,650 --> 00:21:45,140
you've set aside.

584
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:48,200
Mathieu: In the comments, complete this sentence:

585
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:50,580
"One thing I'd like to stop

586
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:53,140
putting off until tomorrow is..."

587
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:55,060
Léa: Or: "Today,

588
00:21:55,060 --> 00:21:57,140
I'm going to take ten minutes to..."

589
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:59,140
Mathieu: One sentence is enough.

590
00:21:59,140 --> 00:22:01,140
Don't be afraid of making mistakes.

591
00:22:01,140 --> 00:22:04,140
It's also by using French

592
00:22:04,140 --> 00:22:06,140
that you learn to express yourself better.

593
00:22:06,140 --> 00:22:08,140
Léa: And if you enjoyed this episode,

594
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:11,140
remember to leave a little thumbs-up,

595
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:13,140
subscribe to The Cozy French

596
00:22:13,140 --> 00:22:15,200
and share this conversation

597
00:22:15,250 --> 00:22:18,140
with someone who's learning French.

598
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:21,140
Mathieu: Thank you so much for spending this time with us.

599
00:22:21,140 --> 00:22:23,140
Before we finish, Léa,

600
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:26,140
if you had to give just one piece of advice

601
00:22:26,140 --> 00:22:29,140
to someone who wants to be more disciplined,

602
00:22:29,140 --> 00:22:31,090
what would it be?

603
00:22:31,140 --> 00:22:34,140
Léa: I'd tell them to start with a promise

604
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:37,140
small enough to be able to keep it,

605
00:22:37,140 --> 00:22:40,140
even on an ordinary day.

606
00:22:40,140 --> 00:22:41,780
Mathieu: No need to become perfect

607
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:43,210
overnight?

608
00:22:43,260 --> 00:22:45,140
Léa: Absolutely not.

609
00:22:45,140 --> 00:22:46,690
Above all, you need to build

610
00:22:46,690 --> 00:22:48,990
realistic habits and learn

611
00:22:48,990 --> 00:22:52,140
to come back to them when you lose your rhythm.

612
00:22:52,140 --> 00:22:53,280
Mathieu: And not forget

613
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:56,140
to rest when it's necessary.

614
00:22:56,140 --> 00:23:00,140
Léa: Exactly. Discipline isn't a punishment.

615
00:23:00,140 --> 00:23:01,040
It's a way

616
00:23:01,040 --> 00:23:03,140
to take better care of our decisions,

617
00:23:03,140 --> 00:23:07,140
our time and what matters to us.

618
00:23:07,140 --> 00:23:08,140
Mathieu: This was Mathieu...

619
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:11,200
Léa: And Léa, from The Cozy French!

620
00:23:11,250 --> 00:23:13,140
Mathieu: We'll see you very soon

621
00:23:13,140 --> 00:23:16,140
for a new conversation in French.

622
00:23:16,140 --> 00:23:19,140
Léa: Take care, go at your own pace,

623
00:23:19,140 --> 00:23:20,070
and remember

624
00:23:20,070 --> 00:23:22,140
that every small commitment you keep

625
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:22,910
can help you

626
00:23:22,910 --> 00:23:25,140
build more self-confidence.

627
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:27,090
Mathieu: See you very soon, dear friends!

628
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:28,930
Léa: Bye for now!
